& [RIS-C01] exact seed roots are one admitted bootstrap-runtime descriptor and one admitted installation-SOP descriptor
& [RIS-C02] every Cantor-managed installed runtime file is one bounded material node reachable from the exact roots
& [RIS-C03] every material node has exact SHA256 bytes kind provenance compatibility target and verifier identities
& [RIS-C04] derived built acquired supplied and generated nodes retain distinct source and transform semantics
& [RIS-C05] external material is content-addressed and a mutable locator never substitutes for expected identity
& [RIS-C06] hidden ambient paths caches environment values current directories tools and network fallback are prohibited inputs
& [RIS-C07] the graph is acyclic complete and producer-unique with no unreachable node or ambiguous target
& [RIS-C08] logical paths are relative normalized bounded and refuse traversal device drive UNC alternate-stream link and case-collision ambiguity
& [RIS-C09] private keys credentials tokens and protected values remain opaque external-custody references and never enter machine forms evidence or logs
& [RIS-C10] operating-system driver firmware hardware transport network and source availability remain explicit prerequisites or unresolved facts
& [RIS-C11] hash correspondence never implies provenance license policy trust compatibility safety semantic truth or activation authority
& [RIS-C12] compilation verification materialization installation activation successor recognition rollback and cleanup remain distinct lifecycle authorities
& [RIS-C13] RIS-P0 is pure supplied-data computation with no filesystem clock process environment network provider model MCP Git workspace persistence or effect API
& [RIS-C14] all counts depths fields bytes text paths nodes edges prerequisites sources transforms receipts and evidence are finitely bounded
& [RIS-C15] canonical JSON is strict duplicate-free unknown-field-free trailing-free and byte normalized
& [RIS-C16] equal inputs yield byte-identical plans and independent verification results with domain-separated self-excluding digests
& [RIS-C17] existing Cantor seed candidate receipt prepared-runtime and boot-session records may be referenced only by exact identity and invariant
& [RIS-C18] no prior contract is reclassified as complete runtime inflation
& [RIS-C19] the first acceptance fixture is small synthetic provider-free and contains no secret private key model or externally acquired byte
& [RIS-C20] source preservation canonical formation satisfaction signature implementation evidence publication and physical commissioning remain separate phase gates

